    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Muslims believe the Quran was revealed orally to Muhammad through the angel Gabriel over some 23 years, from 610 CE, and was later compiled and given a standard text; modern scholars debate how and when its final form was fixed.</li><li>It has 114 chapters arranged roughly by decreasing length rather than in the order of revelation, and it is recited in Arabic in prayer, with the whole text memorised by those called hafiz.</li><li>Its meaning has been explained by centuries of commentary (tafsir), its text has been copied in many scripts and printed since the 16th century, and it has been translated into over a hundred languages.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moses">Moses</a> is named 136 times in the Quran, more often than any other individual, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> is named more often than Muhammad is.</p></aside>
    </section>

